[profiles.guide]
notes = '''Hold {select} and {start} together to pause the gyro while you reposition the controller. Hold {start} to switch the gyro off or on, and hold {r3} to recenter it.
Flick stick: push the right stick {rs} toward where you want to face and the view turns to it; turn it around the rim to keep turning. The gyro aims up, down and finely.
{start} (Escape) opens the game's menu.
Hold {rt} to grab and carry; {rb} pushes what you hold away and {lb} pulls it closer. {lt} is the right mouse button, which turns a held object in the default keys.
{south} interacts; hold {south} to sprint while you move. {east} jumps, {west} tumbles and {l3} toggles crouch. The game has no walk key.
{left}, {up} and {right} take out inventory slots 1, 2 and 3. Hold {down} to talk if you set voice chat to push-to-talk.
Hold {select} for the map. {north} opens chat: type with the on-screen keyboard, {guide} + {west}.
Multiplayer: the game has no anti-cheat, and the pad reaches it as an ordinary keyboard and mouse.
These keys are written from memory and not checked in the game (the right mouse button, tumble, chat and push-to-talk especially). Compare them with Settings → Controls and change the buttons here to match. The gyro's real-world turn is a guess; adjust it in Quick settings until a full turn of the controller turns you all the way round.'''

